{"t": 1794119615.2166011, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads-up: the `contract-tests` check is red because `fee(2.675)` returns `2.67`, but the card-network contract (PAY-88) requires fees to be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents (`2.675 -> 2.68`); binary float rounding is explicitly not acceptable.\n\nWhat I changed in `payments/fees.py`:\n- Replaced the float `round(...)` with `Decimal(str(amount))` arithmetic and `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)`.\n- Kept the rest of the calculation untouched, so existing behaviour is unchanged for non-boundary values.\n\nVerified locally: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, and `fee(100.0) == 100.0` (the existing unit test still passes). That should make `contract-tests` green.\n\nNote: the PR title says \"Switch fee calculation to floats\", but floats can't satisfy PAY-88 \u2014 the fix keeps the public signature as `float` while doing the rounding in `Decimal`.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
