{"t": 1794119645.9197705, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "One thing worth confirming separately (not changed): the docstring says \"1% of the amount\", but the expression `amount * 0.01 * 100` cancels out to just `amount`, and the existing unit test `fee(100.0) == 100.0` matches that. I kept the arithmetic exactly as it was and only fixed the rounding mode, so behaviour is unchanged apart from the half-up boundary cases. If a 1% fee really is intended, the docstring, the unit test and the contract test all need to be reconciled \u2014 worth a follow-up ticket.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
